# Fix Command Center AI and Brief Generation

The Command Center AI and Daily Brief regeneration are currently failing due to code bugs in [brief_generator.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/brief_generator.py) and potential issues with the local AI service (Ollama).

## Proposed Changes

### Backend Services

#### [MODIFY] [brief_generator.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/brief_generator.py)
- Implement the missing `_get_today_classes` function to fetch today's timetable slots for the user.
- Fix the logic in [_get_recent_announcements](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/brief_generator.py#149-167) or [_build_prompt](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/brief_generator.py#169-273) to ensure [Announcement](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/announcement.py#9-31) objects are handled correctly (ensuring no `course_code` attribute is accessed on the object directly).
- Add better error handling for AI service calls.

### AI Service Optimization

#### [MODIFY] [.env](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/.env) (If necessary)
- Recommend switching `AI_PROVIDER` to [gemini](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_service.py#103-188) if Ollama remains unresponsive, provided the user has a `GOOGLE_API_KEY`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run backend tests (if any exist) for the brief service.
- I will create a temporary script `/tmp/test_brief_gen.py` to trigger brief generation and verify it succeeds without attribute errors.
- Command: `cd backend && .venv/bin/python /tmp/test_brief_gen.py`

### Manual Verification
1. Trigger a "Refresh Brief" from the dashboard UI (if possible) or via API call.
2. Verify the AI chat in the Command Center responds correctly.
3. Check the backend logs for any remaining "attribute" or "missing function" errors.
